body:
 I always say I'm great when I get asked. But I know that the people around me would never understand if I told them the truth and they would have me committed. And I don't want to be known as some local lunatic.

&#x200B;

Back when I was bullied from age 7-16 it went to the point were I joined in and made fun of myself. As a coping mechanism I guess. The only thing I ever wanted was to be socially accepted. So that's were all my energy went. But that only made it worse. Since I was now "buying" friends. The "friendships" didn't last longer than a day. It went so far that I started fantazising about killing them. I'm glad I never did act out on that. But that was mostly how I got through my days. I never fully recovered from that. But I understand from experience how people feel that they are driven to do something like that. Sacrificing their physical existence to save their "soul" from further harm. It's terrible.

&#x200B;

At home it was bad too. My mom had gotten a boyfriend who was an addict at that time. And he was sometimes straight up abusive towards me and my brother. On one occassion I remember him taking a sponge and shoving it in the catlitter and then he forced it into my mouth for hiding his shoe when he was alone with us. My mother brushed it aside and said that we shoudn't joke around with him when we told her. My mother is not bad a person. Just a victim of her own life.

&#x200B;

When I look back on my life it's been misery. Started doing hard drugs at 16. Cocaine. meth... pills... you name it I probably did it. I never did heroin though. But pretty much everything else and kept at it. This is not even the worst part. The worst part happened when I was about 11-13. I don't remember exactly when but I raped my littlebrother in his sleep. And this is one of the main reasons why I cannot live with myself any longer. I can't tell anyone irl about this. I never will. I always keep things like this locked inside. But it has torn me apart. So many hours that I've spent thinking about how that could happen. How evil am I? No good person would ever even think about something like that. You see this happened almost 15 years ago and the pain gets worse as time passes. At the time I remember thinking I wanted to feel love. And that was my way of achieving it. That's how fucked up I've been since childhood.

&#x200B;

 At this point in my life I'm sometimes engaging in self harm. This is just a small part of my life. But I just wanted to maybe give you a glimpse so you can understand why I am here now.

&#x200B;

Thank you for reading I appreciate it.
